A||||9||Bob Englert||Cheap gas on I-95||||1||
Z||000000||Bob Englert||03-20-2001||12:22 PM||||I just got back from Daytona to visit a college with my daughter.  For those driving down to the Fiero show this weekend I thought I could share some of the gas deals I found.<P>Florence, SC, exit 164 - several of the large truck stops at this exit had regular for 125.9/gal.<P>Port Wendworth, GA - exit 109(?) I got gas at Speedway car and truck stop for 117.9/gal!<P>Kingsland, GA - Exit 1,3,6 - gas here is about 117.9 - 121.9 The cheapest is at the last GA exit at a truck stop.  <P>Gas in FL is much more expensive, typically 135.9 and about 145.9 in Daytona at the stations near the track.<P>Wish I could have made the trip this coming weekend.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl<p>[This message has been edited by Bob Englert (edited 03-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||03-20-2001||12:39 PM||||Bob, will you ship us Californians some of that 117.9 gas??? It's running 167.9 to 187.9 and higher out here!!! Maybe with the savings on the difference I could afford to make it to Daytona!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hank is Here||03-20-2001||12:55 PM||||a little to the west on my way down to Louisania this past weekend, 81, 40, 59 and a few others.  My best price was 1.239  Here in state college it is running about 1.299.  not bad<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||03-20-2001||02:59 PM||||Exit 107 in NC on I-95 is always a good place to stop. The Shell station is well-lit, safe, and the bathrooms are always clean. The exit is called Truck Stop Rd. A mile or two into town there's a used car lot on the right that always has Fieros!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=1676320&p=20236791"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Formula||03-21-2001||09:16 AM||||its about 1.20 to 1.40 here||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroJoe||03-21-2001||09:39 AM||||Gas jumps around so much up here.  It will get down to 1.15, and then the next day go up to 1.48 and come right back down within 2 days.  I always seem to time it right though, get the gas on the downside.<P>Down in jackson (30 min south of me) I heard it went down to 1.05!!<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||PatrickB||03-21-2001||10:29 PM||||Bob,<P>If you dont mind me asking, what college were you looking at?<BR>Im attending Embry-Riddle in the fall which is in Daytona.<P>Pat||||reg||5
Z||000007||Bob Englert||03-22-2001||01:30 PM||||Pat:<P>We were looking at Embry-Riddle.  Megan is interested in Aerospace Engineering and will be taking a class for rising HS senoirs at ERAU this summer.  She is a Junior now and is very interested in the school when she graduates.  <P>Are you going for engineering or flight training?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000008||PatrickB||03-22-2001||07:14 PM||||Im going to transfer down this Fall for aero science which is flight training.  I've already sent in my tuition deposit and housing contract.  I have a friend who used to go there and have visited a couple of times myself.  One was for the Open House in September.<P>They have a very good reputation for their flight training and I think they were picked as the number one engineering school in the country.  I know the airlines and aerospace companies look very highly on Embry-Riddle which is why I chose it.<P>Some good scholarship opportunities for your daughter if she has good grades although aero sci majors dont get any.  Comes in handy with that hefty tuition.  <P>I may not be of much help now since Im not enrolled in any classes yet but if you or your daughter have any questions feel free to contact me. My email is fierogt@optonline.com<P>Pat||||reg||14
